  $q74046${"mode":"reading","level":"B1","format":"text","topic":"Hobbies","title":"A Game on the Kitchen Table","story":"Every Tuesday evening, Imani set a chessboard on the kitchen table. Her uncle Theo was teaching her the pieces. She already knew the pawns moved one square, but the knights still confused her. Theo showed the L shape with two coins and a bean. Imani tried the move and captured his bishop. She grinned, then saw that her queen was in danger. Theo did not let her take the move back. He said a real game had no second chances. They played until the soup was ready. Imani wrote the knight move on a card and taped it inside the box. Next week she wanted to remember it without help.","dialogue":[],"vocabulary":[{"word":"chessboard","definition":"the board used for the game of chess"},{"word":"pawns","definition":"the smallest chess pieces, which move one square"},{"word":"knights","definition":"chess pieces that jump in an L shape"},{"word":"captured","definition":"took an opponent piece off the board"},{"word":"bishop","definition":"a chess piece that moves on a diagonal"},{"word":"queen","definition":"the strongest piece in chess"}],"quiz":[{"question":"When does Imani usually set up the game?","options":["After school on Friday","On Sunday morning","On Tuesday evening","Only in the winter"],"correctAnswer":"On Tuesday evening","explanation":"Every Tuesday evening she set a chessboard on the kitchen table.","supportingSentence":"Every Tuesday evening, Imani set a chessboard on the kitchen table.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"Which pieces still confused Imani?","options":["The coins on the shelf","The knights","The pawns","The soup bowls"],"correctAnswer":"The knights","explanation":"She knew the pawns, but the knights still confused her.","supportingSentence":"She already knew the pawns moved one square, but the knights still confused her.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"Where did Imani put the note about the knight move?","options":["Inside the box",