"},{"question":"In this story, what does heel mean?","options":["A kind of plaster","The front of a boot","The top of a hill","The back part of the foot"],"correctAnswer":"The back part of the foot","explanation":"His heel began to sting, and that is the back of the foot.","supportingSentence":"By the second hill his heel began to sting.","skill":"vocabulary"},{"question":"Why did Yusuf lace the boot more loosely?","options":["So the sore heel would not be pressed","So the plaster would fall off","So the friend could wear it","So he could run ahead"],"correctAnswer":"So the sore heel would not be pressed","explanation":"He had a blister on his heel, so a looser boot would press it less.","supportingSentence":"Yusuf pressed the plaster on and laced the boot more loosely.","skill":"inference"}],"wordCount":102,"questionCount":5}$q50515$::jsonb,
