  $q5194${"topic":"culture_food","wordCount":106,"questionCount":5}$q5194$::jsonb,
  $q63822${"mode":"reading","level":"B1","format":"text","topic":"Culture & Food","title":"Noodles before the New Year","story":"On the night before the new year, Kenji and his grandmother made long noodles. She said the long strands stood for a long life. Kenji boiled water and watched the pot so it would not spill. His grandmother added greens, ginger, and a little soy. They set two bowls on a red cloth. Kenji tried to slurp the way she did and laughed when a strand hit his chin. She told him to slow down and taste the ginger. Neighbours knocked later and shared oranges. Kenji packed a small box of noodles for his teacher. The meal was simple, but the story in it was old.","dialogue":[],"vocabulary":[{"word":"noodles","definition":"long thin strips of cooked dough"},{"word":"strands","definition":"single long pieces"},{"word":"ginger","definition":"a sharp hot root used in cooking"},{"word":"slurp","definition":"to eat or drink with a loud sucking sound"},{"word":"cloth","definition":"a piece of material used as a cover"},{"word":"oranges","definition":"round sweet fruit with a thick skin"}],"quiz":[{"question":"What did the long noodles stand for?","options":["A long life","A new pair of shoes","A short school day","A closed shop"],"correctAnswer":"A long life","explanation":"His grandmother said the long strands stood for a long life.","supportingSentence":"She said the long strands stood for a long life.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What did Kenji do so the pot would not spill?","options":["He hid it","He watched it","He put it outside","He gave it to the neighbours"],"correctAnswer":"He watched it","explanation":"He watched the pot so it would not spill.","supportingSentence":"Kenji boiled water and watched the pot so it would not spill.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"Who received a small box of noodles?","options":["His teacher","The shop keeper","A stranger on the bus","The neighbours only"],"correctAnswer":"His teacher","explanation":"Kenji packed a small box of noodles for his teacher.","supportingSentence":"Kenji packed a small box of noodles for his teacher.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"In this story, what does slurp mean?","options":["To cook very slowly","To share fruit","To fold a red cloth","To eat with a loud sucking sound"],"correctAnswer":"To eat with a loud sucking sound","explanation":"Kenji tried to slurp the noodles the way his grandmother did.","supportingSentence":"Kenji tried to slurp the way she did and laughed when a strand hit his chin.","skill":"vocabulary"},{"question":"Why did his grandmother tell him to slow down?","options":["So he could taste the ginger","So the noodles would break","So the neighbours would leave","So the pot would spill"],"correctAnswer":"So he could taste the ginger","explanation":"She told him to slow down and taste the ginger.","supportingSentence":"She told him to slow down and taste the ginger.","skill":"inference"}],"wordCount":106,"questionCount":5}$q63822$::jsonb,
