  'text',
  $q4839${"topic":"daily life","wordCount":66,"questionCount":5}$q4839$::jsonb,
  $q18514${"mode":"reading","level":"C1","format":"text","topic":"Daily Life","title":"A Setting, Not a Sacrifice","story":"When the new intercom stayed open after every delivery, Farah heard the stairwell all evening. She asked the installer to shorten the release rather than mute her handset, because muting would also hide a genuine call. He cut the open interval and tested it with her. Parcels arrived. The flat stayed quiet unless someone meant to speak. A setting, not a sacrifice, had settled the dispute.","dialogue":[],"vocabulary":[{"word":"intercom","definition":"A device for speaking to someone at the door"},{"word":"release","definition":"The part that kept the line open after a buzz"},{"word":"mute","definition":"To turn the sound off"},{"word":"handset","definition":"The part of the phone she held or answered"},{"word":"interval","definition":"The length of time something stays open"},{"word":"sacrifice","definition":"Giving up something important"}],"quiz":[{"question":"What change did Farah request from the installer?","options":["A shorter time with the line left open","An end to parcel deliveries","A handset that stayed silent all evening","A louder stairwell for every call"],"correctAnswer":"A shorter time with the line left open","explanation":"She asked him to shorten the release instead of muting the handset.","supportingSentence":"She asked the installer to shorten the release rather than mute her handset, because muting would also hide a genuine call.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What continued after the open interval was cut?","options":["The stairwell noise lasted all evening","Parcels still came","The installer removed the handset","Genuine calls were hidden"],"correctAnswer":"Parcels still came","explanation":"The story says parcels arrived after he tested the shorter interval.","supportingSentence":"Parcels arrived.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"Why was muting the handset a poor fix?","options":["It would have hidden a real call as well as the noise","The building had banned genuine callers","Parcels had to be carried up a silent stair","The installer could visit only after midnight"],"correctAnswer":"It would have hidden a real call as well as the noise","explanation":"Muting would have stopped the noise and also stopped a call she still needed to hear.","supportingSentence":"She asked the installer to shorten the release rather than mute her handset, because muting would also hide a genuine call.","skill":"inference"},{"question":"What does interval mean in this passage?","options":["A parcel left beside the door","A person who installs locks","A dispute between neighbours","The stretch of time the line stayed open"],"correctAnswer":"The stretch of time the line stayed open","explanation":"He cut the open interval, meaning he reduced how long the intercom stayed live.","supportingSentence":"He cut the open interval and tested it with her.","skill":"vocabulary"},{"question":"Why does the writer contrast a setting with a sacrifice?","options":["To show the fix was an adjustment rather than a loss","To suggest the installer muted the whole building","To prove parcels should stop after dusk","To argue that stairwells ought to stay noisy"],"correctAnswer":"To show the fix was an adjustment rather than a loss","explanation":"The closing line says a setting, rather than a sacrifice, settled the dispute.","supportingSentence":"A setting, not a sacrifice, had settled the dispute.","skill":"intent"}],"wordCount":66,"questionCount":5}$q18514$::jsonb,
  '69cbe324b03193be6ae294ddb2eb976b27fc68c6c8c5416c0223b56c4c104aa5',
  true
) on conflict (content_hash) do nothing;

insert into public.exercise_bank (
  id, kind, level, exercise_type, dimensions, payload, content_hash, active
) values (
  'd81f27ad-e9d5-470f-aa08-e075002d6798'::uuid,
  'reading',
  'C1',
  'text',
  $q4839${"topic":"daily life","wordCount":66,"questionCount":5}$q4839$::jsonb,
  $q22713${"mode":"reading","level":"C1","format":"text","topic":"Daily Life","title":"Cold Rooms and a Late Boost","story":"The shared boiler ran until midnight because nobody wanted to be the person who cut it. After the quarterly bill, Denis proposed an earlier cutoff and a manual boost for late shifts. Two nurses objected until he showed the boost would cover their return. The timer changed, and the next bill fell. Their objection had been about coming home to cold rooms, not about defending waste.","dialogue":[],"vocabulary":[{"word":"boiler","definition":"The heater that supplied the building with hot water or heat"},{"word":"quarterly","definition":"Happening every three months"},{"word":"cutoff","definition":"The time when a system is switched off"},{"word":"boost","definition":"An extra period of heat turned on by hand"},{"word":"objected","definition":"Said they were against the plan"},{"word":"waste","definition":"Using something carelessly when it is not needed"}],"quiz":[{"question":"What extra heat did Denis offer to people on late shifts?","options":["A lower bill and no heat at all","A boiler that ran without any timer","A manual boost to cover their return","Cold rooms as a lesson in saving"],"correctAnswer":"A manual boost to cover their return","explanation":"He proposed a manual boost for late shifts and showed it would cover their return.","supportingSentence":"After the quarterly bill, Denis proposed an earlier cutoff and a manual boost for late shifts.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What happened to the bill after the timer changed?","options":["The next bill doubled","The bill stayed high until midnight","The next bill fell","The bill was cancelled outright"],"correctAnswer":"The next bill fell","explanation":"Once the timer changed, the following bill fell.","supportingSentence":"The timer changed, and the next bill fell.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What does the ending reveal about the nurses?","options":["They wanted heat on return, not waste for its own sake","They refused every kind of manual control","They preferred midnight cold to any boost","They hoped the quarterly bill would rise"],"correctAnswer":"They wanted heat on return, not waste for its own sake","explanation":"Their objection was about coming home to cold rooms, so they were not trying to protect waste.","supportingSentence":"Their objection had been about coming home to cold rooms, not about defending waste.","skill":"inference"},{"question":"What is a boost in this passage?","options":["A cut that leaves the boiler off all night","A complaint about a cold flat","A bill that arrives every three months","Extra heat that can be turned on by hand"],"correctAnswer":"Extra heat that can be turned on by hand","explanation":"The manual boost is the extra heat Denis offered for people finishing late.","supportingSentence":"After the quarterly bill, Denis proposed an earlier cutoff and a manual boost for late shifts.","skill":"vocabulary"},{"question":"Why does the writer mention the quarterly bill?","options":["To suggest midnight was the cheapest hour","To prove the nurses owned the boiler","To show what pushed Denis to change the timer","To argue that late shifts should be abolished"],"correctAnswer":"To show what pushed Denis to change the timer","explanation":"The proposal comes immediately after the quarterly bill, so the bill is the prompt.","supportingSentence":"After the quarterly bill, Denis proposed an earlier cutoff and a manual boost for late shifts.","skill":"intent"}],"wordCount":66,"questionCount":5}$q22713$::jsonb,
  'd81f27ade9d5e70f0a08e075002d6798c53fbaa2ef039dcdf8d37408022c6218',
  true
) on conflict (content_hash) do nothing;

insert into public.exercise_bank (
  id, kind, level, exercise_type, dimensions, payload, content_hash, active
) values (
  'b4bcabd4-a41d-477c-a6ea-7a6d709382e8'::uuid,
  'reading',
  'C1',
  'text',
  $q5330${"topic":"school_college","wordCount":62,"questionCount":5}$q5330$::jsonb,
  $q46116${"mode":"reading","level":"C1","format":"text","topic":"School / College","title":"A Warmer Slot for the Panel","story":"The department listed oral slots alphabetically, leaving Malik last after a wait that dulled his examples. He asked to join the students who shared his case, so the context stayed warm for the panel. Professor Shah agreed, provided Malik heard none of the earlier answers. He waited outside and entered with that cluster. Feedback noted sharper comparisons than his previous solo slot.","dialogue":[],"vocabulary":[{"word":"alphabetically","definition":"In the order of the letters of the names"},{"word":"dulled","definition":"Made less sharp or lively"},{"word":"context","definition":"The surrounding information needed to understand something"},{"word":"panel","definition":"The group of examiners hearing the talks"},{"word":"cluster","definition":"A small group treated together"},{"word":"comparisons","definition":"Judgments about how things differ or match"}],"quiz":[{"question":"Why did Malik’s oral slot fall at the end?","options":["The slots were listed in alphabetical order","The panel wanted a colder context","He had asked to hear every earlier answer","His solo slot had already been judged sharper"],"correctAnswer":"The slots were listed in alphabetical order","explanation":"The department listed the slots alphabetically, and that left him last.","supportingSentence":"The department listed oral slots alphabetically, leaving Malik last after a wait that dulled his examples.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What condition did Professor Shah attach to the move?","options":["He had to present without a case at all","Malik must not hear the answers given before his","Comparisons had to be shorter than before","The panel would mark only the wait outside"],"correctAnswer":"Malik must not hear the answers given before his","explanation":"Shah agreed only if Malik heard none of the earlier answers.","supportingSentence":"Professor Shah agreed, provided Malik heard none of the earlier answers.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What does the sharper feedback suggest about the grouping?","options":["Waiting outside removed the need for examples","Solo slots are marked more kindly than groups","The panel could compare work while the shared case was still fresh","Alphabetical order always produces higher marks"],"correctAnswer":"The panel could compare work while the shared case was still fresh","explanation":"Sharper comparisons than his solo slot fit the aim of keeping the shared case warm for the panel.","supportingSentence":"Feedback noted sharper comparisons than his previous solo slot.","skill":"inference"},{"question":"What does cluster mean in this passage?","options":["A long wait in alphabetical order","The corridor outside the exam room","A mark given for a solo slot","The group of students who shared his case"],"correctAnswer":"The group of students who shared his case","explanation":"He entered with that cluster, the students he had asked to join.","supportingSentence":"He waited outside and entered with that cluster.","skill":"vocabulary"},{"question":"Why does the writer mention the dulled examples?","options":["To show the harm of waiting until the very end","To suggest alphabetical lists are forbidden","To prove the panel disliked his case","To argue that corridors should be silent"],"correctAnswer":"To show the harm of waiting until the very end","explanation":"The dull examples explain why being last was a problem worth fixing.","supportingSentence":"The department listed oral slots alphabetically, leaving Malik last after a wait that dulled his examples.","skill":"intent"}],"wordCount":62,"questionCount":5}$q46116$::jsonb,
  'b4bcabd4a41dd77c66ea7a6d709382e82e7cb971efc2d431179da13a49e79fdc',
  true
) on conflict (content_hash) do nothing;

insert into public.exercise_bank (
  id, kind, level, exercise_type, dimensions, payload, content_hash, active
) values (
  '6419eec7-dec3-440d-aa51-31f6c849b2cc'::uuid,
  'reading',
  'C1',
  'text',
  $q5330${"topic":"school_college","wordCount":62,"questionCount":5}$q5330$::jsonb,
  $q43920${"mode":"reading","level":"C1","format":"text","topic":"School / College","title":"Access ahead of Habit","story":"Anika arrived early to claim the window seat, then gave it up when she saw Luis used it to follow the board. From the back she missed two formulas and copied them from his notes. Their tutor noticed the swap and asked why. Anika said access mattered more than habit. The tutor left seating open, provided nobody treated a chair as property.","dialogue":[],"vocabulary":[{"word":"claim","definition":"To take something as if it were yours"},{"word":"formulas","definition":"Mathematical statements written on the board"},{"word":"swap","definition":"An exchange of one place or thing for another"},{"word":"access","definition":"The chance to reach or see what is needed"},{"word":"habit","definition":"Something a person usually does"},{"word":"property","definition":"Something a person owns"}],"quiz":[{"question":"Why had Luis been using the window seat?","options":["He had bought the chair as property","He arrived later than the rest of the class","He used it to follow the board","He wanted to copy Anika’s notes"],"correctAnswer":"He used it to follow the board","explanation":"Anika gave up the seat when she saw he used it to follow the board.","supportingSentence":"Anika arrived early to claim the window seat, then gave it up when she saw Luis used it to follow the board.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What did Anika miss while sitting at the back?","options":["The tutor’s question about the swap","Her claim on the window chair","Notes from a different class","Two formulas"],"correctAnswer":"Two formulas","explanation":"From the back she missed two formulas and later copied them.","supportingSentence":"From the back she missed two formulas and copied them from his notes.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What did Anika’s reply reveal about her move?","options":["Luis seeing the board mattered more than her usual seat","She hoped to hide the formulas she had missed","The tutor had ordered her to the back before class","She believed each chair should be private property"],"correctAnswer":"Luis seeing the board mattered more than her usual seat","explanation":"Saying that access mattered more than habit shows she gave up her usual seat so he could see.","supportingSentence":"Anika said access mattered more than habit.","skill":"inference"},{"question":"What does claim mean at the start of the passage?","options":["To complain about the writing on the board","To take the seat as though it were hers","To close the seminar before the end","To copy formulas from a classmate"],"correctAnswer":"To take the seat as though it were hers","explanation":"She arrived early to claim the window seat, meaning to take it for herself.","supportingSentence":"Anika arrived early to claim the window seat, then gave it up when she saw Luis used it to follow the board.","skill":"vocabulary"},{"question":"Why does the writer include the condition about property?","options":["To explain why two formulas were hidden","To argue that notes can replace the board","To show the tutor allowed choice but not ownership of seats","To prove Luis had purchased the window chair"],"correctAnswer":"To show the tutor allowed choice but not ownership of seats","explanation":"Open seating with nobody treating a chair as property sets choice without ownership.","supportingSentence":"The tutor left seating open, provided nobody treated a chair as property.","skill":"intent"}],"wordCount":62,"questionCount":5}$q43920$::jsonb,
  '6419eec7dec3a40d7a5131f6c849b2cc1f38125af65b0fa96f3266e4b9c18a2e',
  true
) on conflict (content_hash) do nothing;

insert into public.exercise_bank (
  id, kind, level, exercise_type, dimensions, payload, content_hash, active
) values (
  '77b62213-03da-4811-a5b6-9c2643097edd'::uuid,
  'reading',
  'C1',
  'text',
  $q4513${"topic":"travel","wordCount":65,"questionCount":5}$q4513$::jsonb,
  $q29062${"mode":"reading","level":"C1","format":"text","topic":"Travel","title":"The Timetable, Not the Phone","story":"When the station clock and her phone disagreed, Ruth trusted the printed timetable and stayed on the platform. The train arrived by the clock, and the guard confirmed that the timetable still governed departures. Her phone had kept the time zone of the city she had left. She corrected it before the next connection. An ignored mismatch would have sent her onward an hour early.","dialogue":[],"vocabulary":[{"word":"disagreed","definition":"Showed two different times"},{"word":"timetable","definition":"The printed list of departure times"},{"word":"governed","definition":"Controlled or decided"},{"word":"departures","definition":"The moments when trains leave"},{"word":"mismatch","definition":"A difference between two things that should agree"},{"word":"connection","definition":"A later train she still needed to catch"}],"quiz":[{"question":"What did Ruth trust when the clock and the phone disagreed?","options":["The city she had just left","The time showing on her phone","The printed timetable","A clock inside the arriving train"],"correctAnswer":"The printed timetable","explanation":"She trusted the printed timetable and stayed on the platform.","supportingSentence":"When the station clock and her phone disagreed, Ruth trusted the printed timetable and stayed on the platform.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"Why was the phone showing the wrong time?","options":["The timetable had been printed in another country","It still used the time zone of the city she had left","The guard had reset it during the journey","The station clock was running an hour fast"],"correctAnswer":"It still used the time zone of the city she had left","explanation":"The phone had kept the time zone of the city she had left.","supportingSentence":"Her phone had kept the time zone of the city she had left.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What would following the phone have done?","options":["It would have sent her on an hour too soon","It would have hidden the printed timetable","It would have put her on a train going back","It would have cancelled the next connection"],"correctAnswer":"It would have sent her on an hour too soon","explanation":"Ignoring the mismatch would have sent her onward an hour early.","supportingSentence":"An ignored mismatch would have sent her onward an hour early.","skill":"inference"},{"question":"What does governed mean about the timetable?","options":["It was painted on the station wall","It had been cancelled after the disagreement","It was folded into the margin of a ticket","It decided which departure times were official"],"correctAnswer":"It decided which departure times were official","explanation":"The guard said the timetable still governed departures, so it set the official leaving times.","supportingSentence":"The train arrived by the clock, and the guard confirmed that the timetable still governed departures.","skill":"vocabulary"},{"question":"Why does the writer end with the mismatch that was avoided?","options":["To suggest Ruth preferred travelling after dark","To prove the guard rewrote the timetable","To show what trusting the wrong time would have cost","To argue that phones should replace station clocks"],"correctAnswer":"To show what trusting the wrong time would have cost","explanation":"The last sentence states the early departure she would have made if she had ignored the difference.","supportingSentence":"An ignored mismatch would have sent her onward an hour early.","skill":"intent"}],"wordCount":65,"questionCount":5}$q29062$::jsonb,
  '77b6221303da4811f5b69c2643097edd2b1276f90e7b6114d0ecd7b1339998f8',
  true
) on conflict (content_hash) do nothing;

insert into public.exercise_bank (
  id, kind, level, exercise_type, dimensions, payload, content_hash, active
) values (
  '4cef2612-8ca4-4320-abc3-56efdab4941b'::uuid,
  'reading',
  'C1',
  'text',
  $q4514${"topic":"travel","wordCount":66,"questionCount":5}$q4514$::jsonb,
  $q16629${"mode":"reading","level":"C1","format":"text","topic":"Travel","title":"Carbon Copy at the Border","story":"At the land border, Pavel was sent back for a second copy of the customs form he had already filled. The officer refused a photograph, because the carbon copy had to travel with the luggage. Pavel rewrote every line from memory and checked the totals. The delay cost him the early bus, yet both sheets were stamped. He later kept a blank form in his coat.","dialogue":[],"vocabulary":[{"word":"customs","definition":"The official check on goods people carry across a border"},{"word":"carbon","definition":"The duplicate sheet made to travel with the bags"},{"word":"luggage","definition":"The bags a traveller carries"},{"word":"totals","definition":"The final amounts written on the form"},{"word":"stamped","definition":"Marked with an official stamp of approval"},{"word":"blank","definition":"Empty, with nothing written on it yet"}],"quiz":[{"question":"Why did the officer refuse a photograph of the form?","options":["The carbon copy had to travel with the luggage","Blank forms were no longer issued there","The totals on the first form were wrong","Pavel had already left on the early bus"],"correctAnswer":"The carbon copy had to travel with the luggage","explanation":"The officer refused a photograph because the carbon copy had to go with the luggage.","supportingSentence":"The officer refused a photograph, because the carbon copy had to travel with the luggage.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What did the delay cost Pavel?","options":["His luggage and his coat","A photograph of the officer","The stamp on both sheets","The early bus"],"correctAnswer":"The early bus","explanation":"The delay cost him the early bus, even though both sheets were stamped.","supportingSentence":"The delay cost him the early bus, yet both sheets were stamped.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What does the blank form in his coat suggest?","options":["He no longer trusted any stamped sheet","He hoped to be hired as a customs officer","He meant to avoid another delay over a missing copy","He expected the bus company to supply forms"],"correctAnswer":"He meant to avoid another delay over a missing copy","explanation":"After losing the early bus for lack of a second copy, keeping a blank form shows he was preparing for the next border.","supportingSentence":"He later kept a blank form in his coat.","skill":"inference"},{"question":"What is a carbon copy in this passage?","options":["A total rewritten from memory","A duplicate sheet that had to go with the bags","A photograph stored on a phone","An official stamp on a bus ticket"],"correctAnswer":"A duplicate sheet that had to go with the bags","explanation":"The carbon copy is the second sheet that had to travel with the luggage.","supportingSentence":"The officer refused a photograph, because the carbon copy had to travel with the luggage.","skill":"vocabulary"},{"question":"Why does the writer say Pavel rewrote the form from memory?","options":["To show he did not have the first copy in his hands","To suggest the officer had lost the luggage","To argue that borders should ban paper","To prove the totals had been false"],"correctAnswer":"To show he did not have the first copy in his hands","explanation":"Rewriting from memory shows the original form was not with him when he was sent back.","supportingSentence":"Pavel rewrote every line from memory and checked the totals.","skill":"intent"}],"wordCount":66,"questionCount":5}$q16629$::jsonb,
  '4cef26128ca4d320cbc356efdab4941bae50690663f870c74d68517d329fb95b',
  true
) on conflict (content_hash) do nothing;

insert into public.exercise_bank (
  id, kind, level, exercise_type, dimensions, payload, content_hash, active
) values (
  'f298b28f-ffd9-4c90-aa49-3c25f2b7d290'::uuid,
  'reading',
  'C1',
  'text',
  $q4591${"topic":"hobbies","wordCount":65,"questionCount":5}$q4591$::jsonb,
  $q21989${"mode":"reading","level":"C1","format":"text","topic":"Hobbies","title":"Pressed on Paper She Owned","story":"Clara stopped pressing flowers in heavy books after a rare daisy stained a library dictionary. She switched to blotting paper and a board kept at home, labelling each specimen with place and date. The method took longer and held less colour, but the books survived. Asked later about the mark, she could point to a change already made. The hobby continued on paper she owned.","dialogue":[],"vocabulary":[{"word":"pressing","definition":"Flattening and drying flowers under weight"},{"word":"stained","definition":"Left a mark that was hard to remove"},{"word":"blotting","definition":"Paper that absorbs moisture"},{"word":"specimen","definition":"One collected example kept for study or display"},{"word":"survived","definition":"Stayed undamaged"},{"word":"mark","definition":"The stain left on the page"}],"quiz":[{"question":"What did the rare daisy do to the library dictionary?","options":["It removed the blotting paper","It made the colours brighter","It stained the dictionary","It became a labelled specimen"],"correctAnswer":"It stained the dictionary","explanation":"She stopped the old method after a rare daisy stained a library dictionary.","supportingSentence":"Clara stopped pressing flowers in heavy books after a rare daisy stained a library dictionary.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"How did the new method compare with pressing in books?","options":["It needed no place and no date","It took longer and kept less colour","It dried the flowers inside library books","It made every specimen brighter than before"],"correctAnswer":"It took longer and kept less colour","explanation":"The new method took longer and held less colour, while the books survived.","supportingSentence":"The method took longer and held less colour, but the books survived.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"Why could Clara answer calmly when asked about the mark?","options":["She had already changed the method that caused it","The library had given her the damaged book","Blotting paper had been banned in the building","The stain had faded before anyone asked"],"correctAnswer":"She had already changed the method that caused it","explanation":"She could point to a change already made, so the cause had been dealt with before the question.","supportingSentence":"Asked later about the mark, she could point to a change already made.","skill":"inference"},{"question":"What is a specimen in this hobby?","options":["A heavy book borrowed from the library","A wooden board used for painting","A stain left on a page","A flower kept as a collected example"],"correctAnswer":"A flower kept as a collected example","explanation":"She labelled each specimen with a place and a date, so a specimen is one of the flowers she kept.","supportingSentence":"She switched to blotting paper and a board kept at home, labelling each specimen with place and date.","skill":"vocabulary"},{"question":"Why does the writer end with paper she owned?","options":["To suggest daisies cannot be dried at home","To prove the library told her to stop collecting","To show the hobby continued without harming borrowed books","To argue that colour matters more than dates"],"correctAnswer":"To show the hobby continued without harming borrowed books","explanation":"Ending on paper she owned shows she kept the hobby while leaving library books alone.","supportingSentence":"The hobby continued on paper she owned.","skill":"intent"}],"wordCount":65,"questionCount":5}$q21989$::jsonb,
  'f298b28fffd9fc900a493c25f2b7d2901bdf5110a39c1fee6fee323f4ab964c8',
  true
) on conflict (content_hash) do nothing;

insert into public.exercise_bank (
  id, kind, level, exercise_type, dimensions, payload, content_hash, active
) values (
  '407320d1-5aca-43db-a558-1bd8cdab0cf2'::uuid,
  'reading',
  'C1',
  'text',
  $q4592${"topic":"hobbies","wordCount":66,"questionCount":5}$q4592$::jsonb,
  $q27042${"mode":"reading","level":"C1","format":"text","topic":"Hobbies","title":"Pitch after Sunset","story":"Before the amateur ensemble recorded, Karim retuned the piano twice because the hall cooled after sunset and the pitch dropped. The conductor wanted one take, so the players sat in silence while Karim worked. He finished with three minutes spare and warned that a long pause would let the strings drift. They recorded without stopping. The recording was imperfect, but the drift he feared never arrived.","dialogue":[],"vocabulary":[{"word":"ensemble","definition":"A small group of musicians playing together"},{"word":"retuned","definition":"Adjusted the notes again so they sounded right"},{"word":"pitch","definition":"How high or low a note sounds"},{"word":"take","definition":"One continuous attempt at a recording"},{"word":"drift","definition":"A slow unwanted change in the notes"},{"word":"imperfect","definition":"Not fully correct, with some faults"}],"quiz":[{"question":"Why did the piano need to be retuned?","options":["The conductor disliked the ensemble","The players arrived after the recording","The recording was already imperfect","The hall cooled and the pitch dropped"],"correctAnswer":"The hall cooled and the pitch dropped","explanation":"Karim retuned the piano because the hall cooled after sunset and the pitch dropped.","supportingSentence":"Before the amateur ensemble recorded, Karim retuned the piano twice because the hall cooled after sunset and the pitch dropped.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"How much spare time remained when the tuning finished?","options":["Three minutes","A long pause","One full take","Until sunset"],"correctAnswer":"Three minutes","explanation":"He finished with three minutes spare.","supportingSentence":"He finished with three minutes spare and warned that a long pause would let the strings drift.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What does the ending show about Karim’s warning?","options":["The recording failed because the strings drifted","The pitch problem he predicted did not happen","The piano was rebuilt during the take","The ensemble paused and tuned again midway"],"correctAnswer":"The pitch problem he predicted did not happen","explanation":"The drift he feared never arrived, even though the recording was imperfect.","supportingSentence":"The recording was imperfect, but the drift he feared never arrived.","skill":"inference"},{"question":"What is a take in this passage?","options":["One continuous attempt at the recording","A tool for tightening strings","A spare minute between pieces","A seat reserved for the conductor"],"correctAnswer":"One continuous attempt at the recording","explanation":"The conductor wanted one take, meaning a single uninterrupted recording.","supportingSentence":"The conductor wanted one take, so the players sat in silence while Karim worked.","skill":"vocabulary"},{"question":"Why does the writer mention the cooling hall?","options":["To show the concert was held outdoors","To prove the conductor arrived after dark","To argue that amateur groups should avoid pianos","To explain why the pitch had fallen"],"correctAnswer":"To explain why the pitch had fallen","explanation":"The cooling hall is given as the reason the pitch dropped and the piano needed retuning.","supportingSentence":"Before the amateur ensemble recorded, Karim retuned the piano twice because the hall cooled after sunset and the pitch dropped.","skill":"intent"}],"wordCount":66,"questionCount":5}$q27042$::jsonb,
  '407320d15aca63db35581bd8cdab0cf224111163723bf8c2050fd0855862533a',
  true
) on conflict (content_hash) do nothing;

