  'text',
  $q5265${"topic":"health_sports","wordCount":63,"questionCount":5}$q5265$::jsonb,
  $q22636${"mode":"reading","level":"C1","format":"text","topic":"Health & Sports","title":"No Baseline for the Stumble","story":"The club skipped baseline balance tests because the equipment arrived late. When Salma stumbled in training, Coach Berg had no earlier score to compare. They paused contact and sent her for the test that afternoon. The number looked ordinary, yet without a baseline it could not show a personal drop. Berg kept her out of contact until a second test matched the first.","dialogue":[],"vocabulary":[{"word":"baseline","definition":"An earlier measurement used for comparison"},{"word":"stumbled","definition":"Lost her footing or balance for a moment"},{"word":"contact","definition":"Training in which players may hit or tackle"},{"word":"ordinary","definition":"Looking normal, with nothing unusual"},{"word":"score","definition":"The number produced by the test"},{"word":"matched","definition":"Was the same as another result"}],"quiz":[{"question":"Why did the club skip the baseline tests?","options":["Contact had already been paused","The second test had already matched the first","The equipment arrived late","Salma refused to be tested"],"correctAnswer":"The equipment arrived late","explanation":"The tests were skipped because the equipment arrived late.","supportingSentence":"The club skipped baseline balance tests because the equipment arrived late.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What restriction stayed until the two tests agreed?","options":["She skipped every training session","She repeated the stumble on purpose","She compared scores for the whole club","She stayed out of contact work"],"correctAnswer":"She stayed out of contact work","explanation":"Berg kept her out of contact until a second test matched the first.","supportingSentence":"Berg kept her out of contact until a second test matched the first.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"Why did a normal-looking result fail to clear her?","options":["There was no earlier score to show whether it was a drop for her","Contact sport does not use numbers at all","The equipment was delivered again that afternoon","The second test was taken by the coach himself"],"correctAnswer":"There was no earlier score to show whether it was a drop for her","explanation":"Without a baseline, an ordinary number could not show a personal drop.","supportingSentence":"The number looked ordinary, yet without a baseline it could not show a personal drop.","skill":"inference"},{"question":"What is a baseline in this passage?","options":["A stumble during a training session","An earlier measurement used for comparison","A piece of equipment that arrived late","A ban on contact sport"],"correctAnswer":"An earlier measurement used for comparison","explanation":"A baseline is the earlier score they lacked, so they could not tell whether the new number was a drop.","supportingSentence":"The number looked ordinary, yet without a baseline it could not show a personal drop.","skill":"vocabulary"},{"question":"Why does the writer mention the late equipment?","options":["To suggest contact should replace balance tests","To argue that afternoon tests are always invalid","To explain why no earlier score existed","To prove Salma had broken the testing kit"],"correctAnswer":"To explain why no earlier score existed","explanation":"The late equipment is the reason the baseline tests were skipped.","supportingSentence":"The club skipped baseline balance tests because the equipment arrived late.","skill":"intent"}],"wordCount":63,"questionCount":5}$q22636$::jsonb,
  '74b2d5502e1a05fc9bd60a0c9c7a4ff118cb629796ce3f9fddde890f9c8557f3',
  true
) on conflict (content_hash) do nothing;

insert into public.exercise_bank (
  id, kind, level, exercise_type, dimensions, payload, content_hash, active
) values (
  '61d21354-a832-4b6e-a8df-3ef2baedc321'::uuid,
  'reading',
  'C1',
  'text',
  $q5268${"topic":"health_sports","wordCount":66,"questionCount":5}$q5268$::jsonb,
  $q74489${"mode":"reading","level":"C1","format":"text","topic":"Health & Sports","title":"Faster than Pride","story":"Salma left her inhaler in her bag, though the plan put it on the bench within a teammate’s reach. She insisted she would feel the tightness in time. Coach Berg pointed to a previous match where she had not. The inhaler moved to the bench, labelled with her name, and she used it at the interval. The tightness never arrived. The plan was faster than pride.","dialogue":[],"vocabulary":[{"word":"inhaler","definition":"A device that delivers medicine for breathing"},{"word":"insisted","definition":"Said something firmly and would not drop it"},{"word":"tightness","definition":"A feeling that the chest or breath is closing"},{"word":"labelled","definition":"Marked with a name so the owner is clear"},{"word":"interval","definition":"The break between parts of the match"},{"word":"pride","definition":"A wish to cope without help"}],"quiz":[{"question":"Where was the inhaler supposed to be kept?","options":["At home, away from the pitch","On the bench within a teammate’s reach","In Salma’s bag until she felt tightness","In the coach’s office after the match"],"correctAnswer":"On the bench within a teammate’s reach","explanation":"The plan put the inhaler on the bench within a teammate’s reach.","supportingSentence":"Salma left her inhaler in her bag, though the plan put it on the bench within a teammate’s reach.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"At what point did she use the inhaler?","options":["During the previous match","After the tightness had already arrived","At the interval","Before any plan had been written"],"correctAnswer":"At the interval","explanation":"She used the inhaler at the interval after it was moved to the bench.","supportingSentence":"The inhaler moved to the bench, labelled with her name, and she used it at the interval.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"Why did Berg mention the earlier match?","options":["The inhaler had been banned after that game","Pride had made the written plan unnecessary","Teammates had hidden the bench that day","She had failed to notice the problem in time before"],"correctAnswer":"She had failed to notice the problem in time before","explanation":"He pointed to a match where she had not felt the tightness in time, which undercuts her confidence.","supportingSentence":"Coach Berg pointed to a previous match where she had not.","skill":"inference"},{"question":"What does interval mean in this passage?","options":["The break between parts of the match","The bag left beside the bench","A previous game she had played","The label stuck on the inhaler"],"correctAnswer":"The break between parts of the match","explanation":"She used the inhaler at the interval, the planned break in the match.","supportingSentence":"The inhaler moved to the bench, labelled with her name, and she used it at the interval.","skill":"vocabulary"},{"question":"Why does the writer say the plan was faster than pride?","options":["To argue that teammates should ignore written plans","To show the written plan prevented trouble sooner than coping alone","To prove the coach cancelled the match","To suggest inhalers work only after pride fails"],"correctAnswer":"To show the written plan prevented trouble sooner than coping alone","explanation":"The closing comparison says the plan beat pride, after she used the inhaler and the tightness never came.","supportingSentence":"The plan was faster than pride.","skill":"intent"}],"wordCount":66,"questionCount":5}$q74489$::jsonb,
  '61d21354a8321b6e98df3ef2baedc321e5b0be3fcd33edd4303d6cb8ad20e658',
  true
) on conflict (content_hash) do nothing;

insert into public.exercise_bank (
  id, kind, level, exercise_type, dimensions, payload, content_hash, active
) values (
  '647d66ec-d2ac-4430-aade-83d9167682d0'::uuid,
  'reading',
  'C1',
  'text',
  $q5151${"topic":"culture_food","wordCount":66,"questionCount":5}$q5151$::jsonb,
  $q38260${"mode":"reading","level":"C1","format":"text","topic":"Culture & Food","title":"A Cue, Not a Scolding","story":"At the feast, Lucia reached for the shared platter before the eldest guest had tasted it, and conversation paused. Mateo did not scold her. He served the elder first and went on talking, giving Lucia a cue rather than a correction. She waited, then followed his order of dishes. He later called the pause courtesy, not punishment. Lucia could repeat the custom without having been shamed.","dialogue":[],"vocabulary":[{"word":"platter","definition":"A large plate shared by several people"},{"word":"eldest","definition":"The oldest person in the group"},{"word":"scold","definition":"To tell someone off angrily"},{"word":"cue","definition":"A quiet signal showing when to act"},{"word":"courtesy","definition":"Polite behaviour that shows respect"},{"word":"custom","definition":"A usual way of doing something in a group"}],"quiz":[{"question":"Who had not yet tasted the platter when Lucia reached for it?","options":["The eldest guest","The cook in the kitchen","Every person at the table","Mateo, the host"],"correctAnswer":"The eldest guest","explanation":"She reached for the platter before the eldest guest had tasted it.","supportingSentence":"At the feast, Lucia reached for the shared platter before the eldest guest had tasted it, and conversation paused.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What did Mateo do instead of scolding Lucia?","options":["He took the platter off the table","He asked Lucia to leave the feast","He announced a punishment to the guests","He served the elder and kept the conversation going"],"correctAnswer":"He served the elder and kept the conversation going","explanation":"He served the elder first and went on talking, giving a cue rather than a correction.","supportingSentence":"He served the elder first and went on talking, giving Lucia a cue rather than a correction.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What did Mateo’s manner suggest he wanted?","options":["For Lucia to learn the order without being humiliated","For conversation to stop until she apologised aloud","For the eldest guest to leave the feast","For the platter to be removed from the room"],"correctAnswer":"For Lucia to learn the order without being humiliated","explanation":"A cue rather than a correction, and no shaming, shows he wanted her to notice the order quietly.","supportingSentence":"He served the elder first and went on talking, giving Lucia a cue rather than a correction.","skill":"inference"},{"question":"What is a cue in this scene?","options":["A punishment for reaching too soon","A quiet signal showing the right moment to act","A loud rebuke in front of the guests","A written list of every dish"],"correctAnswer":"A quiet signal showing the right moment to act","explanation":"He gave her a cue by serving the elder and continuing to talk, instead of correcting her aloud.","supportingSentence":"He served the elder first and went on talking, giving Lucia a cue rather than a correction.","skill":"vocabulary"},{"question":"Why does the writer report that the pause was courtesy, not punishment?","options":["To show the quiet moment was meant to teach rather than shame","To argue that feasts should have no customs","To suggest the elder refused every dish","To prove Lucia had broken a law"],"correctAnswer":"To show the quiet moment was meant to teach rather than shame","explanation":"Calling the pause courtesy rather than punishment frames it as respectful teaching.","supportingSentence":"He later called the pause courtesy, not punishment.","skill":"intent"}],"wordCount":66,"questionCount":5}$q38260$::jsonb,
  '647d66ecd2ac04301ade83d9167682d027aa6c257ed1d70ebdd15939b7664ada',
  true
) on conflict (content_hash) do nothing;

insert into public.exercise_bank (
  id, kind, level, exercise_type, dimensions, payload, content_hash, active
) values (
  'fd51d3b9-f26a-49b3-acf2-3ff10b0d764d'::uuid,
  'reading',
  'C1',
  'text',
  $q5147${"topic":"culture_food","wordCount":62,"questionCount":5}$q5147$::jsonb,
  $q25599${"mode":"reading","level":"C1","format":"text","topic":"Culture & Food","title":"The Second Pouring","story":"At the tasting, guests refused the second pouring, thinking it meant the first had disappointed. Mateo explained that the smaller cooler cup was for conversation, not a correction. Lucia waited, then accepted, and the talk outlasted the meal. He later set a card by the pot so visitors would not mistake courtesy for criticism. A custom left unexplained looks like a judgment.","dialogue":[],"vocabulary":[{"word":"pouring","definition":"A serving of the drink put into the cup"},{"word":"disappointed","definition":"Failed to please, or seemed not good enough"},{"word":"correction","definition":"An act meant to put a mistake right"},{"word":"outlasted","definition":"Went on longer than something else"},{"word":"courtesy","definition":"A polite gesture of welcome"},{"word":"unexplained","definition":"Not made clear to the people watching"}],"quiz":[{"question":"What did the guests think the second pouring meant?","options":["That the first cup had disappointed the host","That the card by the pot was a joke","That they were expected to leave before the meal","That cooler drinks were banned at the tasting"],"correctAnswer":"That the first cup had disappointed the host","explanation":"They refused the second pouring because they thought it meant the first had disappointed.","supportingSentence":"At the tasting, guests refused the second pouring, thinking it meant the first had disappointed.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What was the smaller cooler cup meant for?","options":["A penalty for poor manners","A written judgment of the guest","A replacement for the whole meal","Conversation, not a correction"],"correctAnswer":"Conversation, not a correction","explanation":"Mateo said the smaller cooler cup was for conversation, not a correction.","supportingSentence":"Mateo explained that the smaller cooler cup was for conversation, not a correction.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What does the long conversation show about the second cup?","options":["It forced the guests to leave before the meal ended","It confirmed that the first pouring had failed","It worked as a prompt for talk, as the host had claimed","It removed any need for a custom that evening"],"correctAnswer":"It worked as a prompt for talk, as the host had claimed","explanation":"The talk lasting longer than the meal shows the second cup did the conversational work Mateo had described.","supportingSentence":"Lucia waited, then accepted, and the talk outlasted the meal.","skill":"inference"},{"question":"What does outlasted mean here?","options":["Was refused by the guests","Lasted longer than the meal","Was poured into a cooler cup","Was mistaken for criticism"],"correctAnswer":"Lasted longer than the meal","explanation":"The talk outlasted the meal, so the conversation continued after the food was finished.","supportingSentence":"Lucia waited, then accepted, and the talk outlasted the meal.","skill":"vocabulary"},{"question":"Why does the writer say an unexplained custom looks like a judgment?","options":["To show why the custom needed to be made clear","To argue that cooler cups are insults","To suggest cards should replace hosts","To prove the first pouring had failed"],"correctAnswer":"To show why the custom needed to be made clear","explanation":"The last line explains the risk that made the card and the explanation necessary.","supportingSentence":"A custom left unexplained looks like a judgment.","skill":"intent"}],"wordCount":62,"questionCount":5}$q25599$::jsonb,
  'fd51d3b9f26a29b32cf23ff10b0d764d275253316b9b3d5ab276bbed03f366aa',
  true
) on conflict (content_hash) do nothing;

insert into public.exercise_bank (
  id, kind, level, exercise_type, dimensions, payload, content_hash, active
) values (
  '3dc4b9cd-b0ed-4b3d-a411-ac81f1fea9ae'::uuid,
  'reading',
  'C1',
  'text',
  $q4943${"topic":"technology","wordCount":65,"questionCount":5}$q4943$::jsonb,
  $q62397${"mode":"reading","level":"C1","format":"text","topic":"Technology","title":"Logs before Any Rollback","story":"When the update locked staff out of the roster, Nadia argued for an immediate rollback. The vendor wanted logs first, warning that reversing blindly could restore the fault. For forty minutes the clinic used a paper list, and two appointments were nearly doubled. Nadia collected the error text before she yielded. The rollback then took minutes, and the vendor’s caution spared them a second outage.","dialogue":[],"vocabulary":[{"word":"roster","definition":"The list of staff or appointments in the system"},{"word":"rollback","definition":"Returning a system to the version used before an update"},{"word":"vendor","definition":"The company that supplied the software"},{"word":"logs","definition":"Records of what the system did"},{"word":"yielded","definition":"Gave way and accepted the other plan"},{"word":"outage","definition":"A period when the system cannot be used"}],"quiz":[{"question":"What did the clinic use while the roster was locked?","options":["The vendor’s private phone","An old roster kept at home","A second software update","A paper list"],"correctAnswer":"A paper list","explanation":"For forty minutes the clinic used a paper list.","supportingSentence":"For forty minutes the clinic used a paper list, and two appointments were nearly doubled.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What did Nadia gather before she yielded?","options":["The error text","Proof of a second outage","The vendor’s complete logs","A list of staff home addresses"],"correctAnswer":"The error text","explanation":"She collected the error text before she yielded.","supportingSentence":"Nadia collected the error text before she yielded.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"Why did the vendor resist an immediate rollback?","options":["The paper list had already doubled every appointment","A second outage had already begun","Undoing the update without information might bring the fault back","Nadia had refused to describe the roster"],"correctAnswer":"Undoing the update without information might bring the fault back","explanation":"The vendor warned that reversing blindly could restore the fault, so the logs had to come first.","supportingSentence":"The vendor wanted logs first, warning that reversing blindly could restore the fault.","skill":"inference"},{"question":"What is an outage in this passage?","options":["A stretch of time when the system could not be used","A paper copy of the day’s appointments","A careful reading of the logs","A request for a faster update"],"correctAnswer":"A stretch of time when the system could not be used","explanation":"A second outage would have been another period when the system failed, which the caution spared them.","supportingSentence":"The rollback then took minutes, and the vendor’s caution spared them a second outage.","skill":"vocabulary"},{"question":"Why does the writer mention the nearly doubled appointments?","options":["To prove the vendor wanted the clinic to close","To explain why Nadia refused every rollback","To suggest paper is more accurate than software","To show the practical cost of the locked roster"],"correctAnswer":"To show the practical cost of the locked roster","explanation":"The doubled appointments show what the lock did to real patients while staff waited.","supportingSentence":"For forty minutes the clinic used a paper list, and two appointments were nearly doubled.","skill":"intent"}],"wordCount":65,"questionCount":5}$q62397$::jsonb,
  '3dc4b9cdb0ed6b3d9411ac81f1fea9aedce424d66060f27897669054dccba14c',
  true
) on conflict (content_hash) do nothing;

insert into public.exercise_bank (
  id, kind, level, exercise_type, dimensions, payload, content_hash, active
) values (
  '88b52d3c-ad08-4e82-a9ed-f46e508648f6'::uuid,
  'reading',
  'C1',
  'text',
  $q4940${"topic":"technology","wordCount":62,"questionCount":5}$q4940$::jsonb,
  $q21904${"mode":"reading","level":"C1","format":"text","topic":"Technology","title":"A Reason Left on the Deletion","story":"The studio inbox let anyone delete a client message. After a booking vanished during a tidy, Sen required every deletion to keep the sender, the time, and a reason. Staff called the extra fields slow and unnecessary. The next missing note was rebuilt from those fields in minutes. Speed had been erasing the only history a client could ask them to prove.","dialogue":[],"vocabulary":[{"word":"inbox","definition":"The shared place where messages arrive"},{"word":"vanished","definition":"Disappeared"},{"word":"deletion","definition":"The act of removing a message"},{"word":"fields","definition":"The separate boxes of information that were saved"},{"word":"rebuilt","definition":"Put back together from the saved details"},{"word":"erasing","definition":"Removing something so it cannot be recovered"}],"quiz":[{"question":"What could any staff member do to a client message at first?","options":["Rebuild it from a written reason","Delete it","Send it only to the studio owner","Keep it for the client forever by rule"],"correctAnswer":"Delete it","explanation":"The inbox let anyone delete a client message.","supportingSentence":"The studio inbox let anyone delete a client message.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What did Sen require a deletion to keep?","options":["The sender, the time, and a reason","A paper copy of every booking","Only the client’s telephone number","The fields staff had already refused"],"correctAnswer":"The sender, the time, and a reason","explanation":"Every deletion had to keep the sender, the time, and a reason.","supportingSentence":"After a booking vanished during a tidy, Sen required every deletion to keep the sender, the time, and a reason.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"Why could the next missing note be rebuilt so quickly?","options":["Staff had stopped deleting messages entirely","The client brought a paper copy within minutes","Speed had created a second inbox","The saved fields still held enough detail to reconstruct it"],"correctAnswer":"The saved fields still held enough detail to reconstruct it","explanation":"The note was rebuilt from those fields, so the required details made the recovery possible.","supportingSentence":"The next missing note was rebuilt from those fields in minutes.","skill":"inference"},{"question":"What does vanished mean in this passage?","options":["Disappeared from the inbox","Was rebuilt the same afternoon","Was proved by the client in court","Grew slower to type"],"correctAnswer":"Disappeared from the inbox","explanation":"The booking vanished during a tidy, meaning it disappeared from the messages.","supportingSentence":"After a booking vanished during a tidy, Sen required every deletion to keep the sender, the time, and a reason.","skill":"vocabulary"},{"question":"Why does the writer end by saying speed had been erasing history?","options":["To argue that reasons should stay blank","To show the cost of deleting without a record","To prove clients never asked for proof","To suggest a tidy inbox is always safer"],"correctAnswer":"To show the cost of deleting without a record","explanation":"The last line names what the old speed had destroyed: the history a client might need proved.","supportingSentence":"Speed had been erasing the only history a client could ask them to prove.","skill":"intent"}],"wordCount":62,"questionCount":5}$q21904$::jsonb,
  '88b52d3cad08ee82f9edf46e508648f6d134fcc3f9264d3715583ee6875336d2',
  true
) on conflict (content_hash) do nothing;

insert into public.exercise_bank (
  id, kind, level, exercise_type, dimensions, payload, content_hash, active
) values (
  'f1c5adfd-dc2f-47a2-a7ec-56b151c779c1'::uuid,
  'reading',
  'C1',
  'text',
  $q4588${"topic":"science","wordCount":64,"questionCount":5}$q4588$::jsonb,
  $q46068${"mode":"reading","level":"C1","format":"text","topic":"Science","title":"Attention in the Tally","story":"Beatriz counted bird visits while knowing which feeder held the new seed, and her tallies favoured it. A colleague called the preference obvious. Beatriz disagreed, because she might have watched that feeder longer. She repeated the count with the labels hidden. The gap shrank, so the first result had measured her attention as well as the birds. Bias had to be removed, not defended.","dialogue":[],"vocabulary":[{"word":"feeder","definition":"A container that offers seed to birds"},{"word":"tallies","definition":"Counts she recorded"},{"word":"preference","definition":"A result that seemed to favour one choice"},{"word":"labels","definition":"Marks showing which feeder was which"},{"word":"gap","definition":"The difference between the two counts"},{"word":"bias","definition":"A slant in the method that pushes the result"}],"quiz":[{"question":"What did Beatriz know during the first count?","options":["How to hide every label in advance","That her colleague would disagree","That the gap would shrink","Which feeder held the new seed"],"correctAnswer":"Which feeder held the new seed","explanation":"She counted while knowing which feeder held the new seed.","supportingSentence":"Beatriz counted bird visits while knowing which feeder held the new seed, and her tallies favoured it.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"How was the second count different?","options":["The labels were hidden","The colleague made the tally","The birds were removed from the garden","A different kind of seed was used"],"correctAnswer":"The labels were hidden","explanation":"She repeated the count with the labels hidden.","supportingSentence":"She repeated the count with the labels hidden.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What did the shrinking gap imply about the first result?","options":["The new seed had lost every effect","The colleague had swapped the feeders","Part of it came from her attention, not only from the birds","Hidden labels attract more visits"],"correctAnswer":"Part of it came from her attention, not only from the birds","explanation":"Once she could not see the labels the gap shrank, so the first result had measured her attention as well as the birds.","supportingSentence":"The gap shrank, so the first result had measured her attention as well as the birds.","skill":"inference"},{"question":"What is a tally in this passage?","options":["A count of the visits she recorded","A label stuck on the new seed","A feeder placed out of sight","A colleague’s spoken opinion"],"correctAnswer":"A count of the visits she recorded","explanation":"Her tallies favoured the known feeder, so a tally is the count she kept.","supportingSentence":"Beatriz counted bird visits while knowing which feeder held the new seed, and her tallies favoured it.","skill":"vocabulary"},{"question":"Why does the writer include the colleague calling the preference obvious?","options":["To prove the second count was unnecessary","To argue that labels should stay visible","To suggest birds cannot be counted","To show the easy explanation Beatriz refused to trust"],"correctAnswer":"To show the easy explanation Beatriz refused to trust","explanation":"The colleague’s “obvious” preference is the reading she tests instead of accepting.","supportingSentence":"A colleague called the preference obvious.","skill":"intent"}],"wordCount":64,"questionCount":5}$q46068$::jsonb,
  'f1c5adfddc2f77a207ec56b151c779c1bb03dffa124dcf1e51b1378e5a9d398d',
  true
) on conflict (content_hash) do nothing;

insert into public.exercise_bank (
  id, kind, level, exercise_type, dimensions, payload, content_hash, active
) values (
  'eb653966-7ccd-4aad-a3d3-6d23c28f3454'::uuid,
  'reading',
  'C1',
  'text',
  $q4590${"topic":"science","wordCount":66,"questionCount":5}$q4590$::jsonb,
  $q26479${"mode":"reading","level":"C1","format":"text","topic":"Science","title":"Less than the Label Claimed","story":"Before counting spores, Omar checked his hand lens against a slide whose marks he already knew. The lens magnified slightly less than the label claimed, so his first tally would have been low. He adjusted the count by the difference and stuck a note on the case. A newer lens arrived weeks later, already calibrated, and he still tested it. Corrected trust did not become automatic.","dialogue":[],"vocabulary":[{"word":"spores","definition":"Tiny reproductive cells he was counting"},{"word":"magnified","definition":"Made something look larger"},{"word":"tally","definition":"The count of what he saw"},{"word":"adjusted","definition":"Changed the number to allow for the error"},{"word":"calibrated","definition":"Checked and set so the measurement is accurate"},{"word":"automatic","definition":"Done without thinking or checking"}],"quiz":[{"question":"What known object did Omar check the lens against?","options":["A slide whose marks he already knew","A newer lens that arrived weeks later","The note he stuck on the case","A tally written by a colleague"],"correctAnswer":"A slide whose marks he already knew","explanation":"He checked the hand lens against a slide whose marks he already knew.","supportingSentence":"Before counting spores, Omar checked his hand lens against a slide whose marks he already knew.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What was wrong with the magnification?","options":["It made the first tally too high","It hid every mark on the slide","It was slightly less than the label claimed","It had already been calibrated that morning"],"correctAnswer":"It was slightly less than the label claimed","explanation":"The lens magnified slightly less than the label claimed, so the first tally would have been low.","supportingSentence":"The lens magnified slightly less than the label claimed, so his first tally would have been low.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"Why did Omar still test the newer lens?","options":["His note had fallen off the old lens","Spores cannot be counted without two lenses","An earlier correction had not made him trust labels on their own","The new lens arrived without any case"],"correctAnswer":"An earlier correction had not made him trust labels on their own","explanation":"He tested the new lens because corrected trust had not become automatic.","supportingSentence":"Corrected trust did not become automatic.","skill":"inference"},{"question":"What is a tally in this passage?","options":["A slide with marks he knew","A note stuck to the case","The claim printed on the label","The count of what he saw through the lens"],"correctAnswer":"The count of what he saw through the lens","explanation":"His first tally would have been low, meaning the count of spores he would have recorded.","supportingSentence":"The lens magnified slightly less than the label claimed, so his first tally would have been low.","skill":"vocabulary"},{"question":"Why does the writer include the note on the case?","options":["To show he left a record of the difference he had found","To prove the newer lens was already broken","To suggest spores should be counted without a lens","To argue that labels are always exact"],"correctAnswer":"To show he left a record of the difference he had found","explanation":"The note sits beside the adjusted count, so the difference is recorded and not only remembered.","supportingSentence":"He adjusted the count by the difference and stuck a note on the case.","skill":"intent"}],"wordCount":66,"questionCount":5}$q26479$::jsonb,
  'eb6539667ccd7aad33d36d23c28f345460ac429ce9058daae5c10914728ea161',
  true
) on conflict (content_hash) do nothing;

insert into public.exercise_bank (
  id, kind, level, exercise_type, dimensions, payload, content_hash, active
) values (
  'b4cd988c-7b8b-4ed3-a3fb-107d975a6838'::uuid,
  'reading',
  'C1',
  'text',
  $q5439${"topic":"economy_finance","wordCount":64,"questionCount":5}$q5439$::jsonb,
  $q29283${"mode":"reading","level":"C1","format":"text","topic":"Economy / Finance","title":"A Price for Hurry","story":"The workshop priced rush jobs at the ordinary rate, then wondered why the evenings vanished. Celia added a surcharge for work promised inside two days and showed it before anyone agreed. Two clients left. Those who stayed either waited or paid for the hurry. Income per hour rose, and the quiet weeks returned. A price that hides urgency teaches people that speed is free.","dialogue":[],"vocabulary":[{"word":"priced","definition":"Set the amount customers would pay"},{"word":"surcharge","definition":"An extra charge added for a special demand"},{"word":"vanished","definition":"Disappeared"},{"word":"hurry","definition":"Work that has to be done very quickly"},{"word":"income","definition":"Money coming in"},{"word":"urgency","definition":"The need for something to be done at once"}],"quiz":[{"question":"Which jobs attracted the new surcharge?","options":["Only the clients who left","Every ordinary job in the workshop","Work promised inside two days","Quiet weeks with no hurry"],"correctAnswer":"Work promised inside two days","explanation":"Celia added a surcharge for work promised inside two days.","supportingSentence":"Celia added a surcharge for work promised inside two days and showed it before anyone agreed.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What could the clients who stayed do?","options":["Set the workshop’s income themselves","Wait, or pay for the hurry","Leave without paying the ordinary rate","Hide the urgency and keep the old price"],"correctAnswer":"Wait, or pay for the hurry","explanation":"Those who stayed either waited or paid for the hurry.","supportingSentence":"Those who stayed either waited or paid for the hurry.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What does the choice given to remaining clients suggest?","options":["Hurry was now optional and no longer bundled into the normal price","Quiet weeks were sold as a separate product","The ordinary rate had been abolished for all work","Everyone had to pay extra even if they waited"],"correctAnswer":"Hurry was now optional and no longer bundled into the normal price","explanation":"They could wait or pay for speed, so hurry had become a priced choice rather than part of the ordinary rate.","supportingSentence":"Those who stayed either waited or paid for the hurry.","skill":"inference"},{"question":"What is a surcharge in this passage?","options":["A client who leaves the workshop","The ordinary rate for a normal job","A quiet week with no orders","An extra charge added for a special demand"],"correctAnswer":"An extra charge added for a special demand","explanation":"The surcharge is the extra amount for work promised inside two days.","supportingSentence":"Celia added a surcharge for work promised inside two days and showed it before anyone agreed.","skill":"vocabulary"},{"question":"Why does the writer say Celia showed the surcharge before anyone agreed?","options":["To suggest two days was too long to wait","To prove the price was hidden until the work ended","To show clients could accept or refuse the cost in advance","To argue that income per hour should fall"],"correctAnswer":"To show clients could accept or refuse the cost in advance","explanation":"Showing the charge before agreement means the cost was known before anyone said yes.","supportingSentence":"Celia added a surcharge for work promised inside two days and showed it before anyone agreed.","skill":"intent"}],"wordCount":64,"questionCount":5}$q29283$::jsonb,
  'b4cd988c7b8b4ed313fb107d975a68389fcb25b7d6de7286077b4901f11b09a0',
  true
) on conflict (content_hash) do nothing;

insert into public.exercise_bank (
  id, kind, level, exercise_type, dimensions, payload, content_hash, active
) values (
  '5f0801c6-6854-47e9-ab20-c3ce1919b091'::uuid,
  'reading',
  'C1',
  'text',
  $q4653${"topic":"mystery","wordCount":62,"questionCount":5}$q4653$::jsonb,
  $q94092${"mode":"reading","level":"C1","format":"text","topic":"Mystery","title":"The Tenth Coat Was Dry","story":"The theatre locked with nine coats and opened with ten. The extra coat was dry, though rain had fallen all evening, and its pocket held no ticket stub. Cameras watched the lobby but not the side aisle. A programme from the later act lay on a seat sold as empty. Rafi decided the visit had been chosen, not forced by the weather.","dialogue":[],"vocabulary":[{"word":"extra","definition":"One more than there should have been"},{"word":"stub","definition":"The small torn remainder of a ticket"},{"word":"lobby","definition":"The entrance hall of the theatre"},{"word":"aisle","definition":"The side passage between the seats"},{"word":"programme","definition":"The printed sheet describing the performance"},{"word":"chosen","definition":"Decided on purpose rather than by chance"}],"quiz":[{"question":"How many coats were there when the theatre opened?","options":["Nine","None in the side aisle","One dry ticket stub","Ten"],"correctAnswer":"Ten","explanation":"The theatre opened with ten coats.","supportingSentence":"The theatre locked with nine coats and opened with ten.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What did the extra coat’s pocket not contain?","options":["A ticket stub","A seam along the edge","A button at the cuff","A dry lining"],"correctAnswer":"A ticket stub","explanation":"Its pocket held no ticket stub.","supportingSentence":"The extra coat was dry, though rain had fallen all evening, and its pocket held no ticket stub.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"Why did a soaked latecomer seem unlikely?","options":["Rafi had dried the coat before the doors opened","The extra coat had stayed dry through an evening of rain","The lobby cameras showed a very wet ticket","The empty seat was outdoors in the storm"],"correctAnswer":"The extra coat had stayed dry through an evening of rain","explanation":"A person driven in by the rain would likely be wet, but the extra coat was dry.","supportingSentence":"The extra coat was dry, though rain had fallen all evening, and its pocket held no ticket stub.","skill":"inference"},{"question":"What is a stub in this passage?","options":["A seat that had been sold as empty","A dry coat left in the lobby","The small remainder of a used ticket","A camera above the side aisle"],"correctAnswer":"The small remainder of a used ticket","explanation":"A ticket stub would be the leftover part of a ticket, and the pocket held none.","supportingSentence":"The extra coat was dry, though rain had fallen all evening, and its pocket held no ticket stub.","skill":"vocabulary"},{"question":"Why does the writer mention that the cameras missed the side aisle?","options":["To prove the lobby stayed closed all evening","To argue that coats should be banned","To suggest the programme was being filmed","To show one way in was not being watched"],"correctAnswer":"To show one way in was not being watched","explanation":"Cameras on the lobby but not the side aisle leave an unwatched route into the theatre.","supportingSentence":"Cameras watched the lobby but not the side aisle.","skill":"intent"}],"wordCount":62,"questionCount":5}$q94092$::jsonb,
  '5f0801c6685447e9eb20c3ce1919b0915f882a94b284cd64cc6a6770ae6a3ea5',
  true
) on conflict (content_hash) do nothing;

insert into public.exercise_bank (
  id, kind, level, exercise_type, dimensions, payload, content_hash, active
) values (
  '630aca91-02aa-4bb6-a555-1c1fe7797d6f'::uuid,
  'reading',
  'C1',
  'text',
  $q4834${"topic":"adventure","wordCount":66,"questionCount":5}$q4834$::jsonb,
  $q4101${"mode":"reading","level":"C1","format":"text","topic":"Adventure","title":"The Cache Left Sealed","story":"The marked cache held the last water before the next well, and the cans were dented but sealed. Farid wanted to drink half and carry the rest. Soraya argued for leaving the cache intact and shortening the midday halt instead. They walked through the hot hours and reached the well with every can unopened. A later party would find the water where the map promised it.","dialogue":[],"vocabulary":[{"word":"cache","definition":"A hidden store left for travellers"},{"word":"sealed","definition":"Closed so the contents stay inside"},{"word":"intact","definition":"Complete and unused"},{"word":"halt","definition":"A stop for rest"},{"word":"unopened","definition":"Still closed, with nothing taken out"},{"word":"promised","definition":"Shown or stated as something people could rely on"}],"quiz":[{"question":"What state were the cans in when they were found?","options":["Dented but sealed","Open and half empty","Missing from the marked place","Too hot to carry"],"correctAnswer":"Dented but sealed","explanation":"The cans were dented but sealed.","supportingSentence":"The marked cache held the last water before the next well, and the cans were dented but sealed.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What did Soraya suggest shortening instead of opening the cans?","options":["The distance to the next well","The hot hours after they arrived","The midday halt","The promise printed on the map"],"correctAnswer":"The midday halt","explanation":"She argued for shortening the midday halt and leaving the cache intact.","supportingSentence":"Soraya argued for leaving the cache intact and shortening the midday halt instead.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"Why keep the cache sealed all the way to the well?","options":["A later group could still find water where the map placed it","The cans were too dented to survive the walk","Soraya hoped to sell the water that night","Farid wanted to drink it beside the well instead"],"correctAnswer":"A later group could still find water where the map placed it","explanation":"They left the cans unopened so a later party would find the water where the map promised it.","supportingSentence":"A later party would find the water where the map promised it.","skill":"inference"},{"question":"What does intact mean in this passage?","options":["Dented beyond repair","Missing from the map","Already half drunk","Complete and unused"],"correctAnswer":"Complete and unused","explanation":"Leaving the cache intact means not opening it or using the water.","supportingSentence":"Soraya argued for leaving the cache intact and shortening the midday halt instead.","skill":"vocabulary"},{"question":"Why does the writer say this cache held the last water before the next well?","options":["To show how serious it was to spend that supply early","To prove the well had already run dry","To suggest the map had been drawn wrong","To argue that hot hours are safer than dawn"],"correctAnswer":"To show how serious it was to spend that supply early","explanation":"Calling it the last water before the next well shows what would be lost if they drank it.","supportingSentence":"The marked cache held the last water before the next well, and the cans were dented but sealed.","skill":"intent"}],"wordCount":66,"questionCount":5}$q4101$::jsonb,
  '630aca9102aa2bb665551c1fe7797d6fad61e7dd9d8cf24a7f5650f65264fe06',
  true
) on conflict (content_hash) do nothing;

insert into public.exercise_bank (
  id, kind, level, exercise_type, dimensions, payload, content_hash, active
) values (
  'afc88a0a-439d-4137-ad78-facd5d49f780'::uuid,
  'reading',
  'C1',
  'text',
  $q4618${"topic":"fantasy","wordCount":66,"questionCount":5}$q4618$::jsonb,
  $q23253${"mode":"reading","level":"C1","format":"text","topic":"Fantasy","title":"Streets the Map Forgot","story":"The tower map redrew itself each dawn and forgot any street nobody had walked the previous day. Lale saw her alley fading after a week indoors. She walked it at dusk, naming each door, and the ink returned by morning. The keeper said the map recorded use, not a promise that places would remain. Unwalked streets became rumours. She added them to a short evening loop.","dialogue":[],"vocabulary":[{"word":"redrew","definition":"Drew again in a changed form"},{"word":"fading","definition":"Growing faint and close to disappearing"},{"word":"ink","definition":"The dark lines that made the streets visible"},{"word":"keeper","definition":"The person who looked after the map"},{"word":"rumours","definition":"Uncertain stories, no longer solid facts"},{"word":"loop","definition":"A short route that comes back to its start"}],"quiz":[{"question":"When did the tower map redraw itself?","options":["Only at dusk","Each dawn","Whenever a rumour began","After a week indoors"],"correctAnswer":"Each dawn","explanation":"The map redrew itself each dawn.","supportingSentence":"The tower map redrew itself each dawn and forgot any street nobody had walked the previous day.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What did Lale do before the ink returned?","options":["She walked the alley at dusk and named the doors","She stayed indoors for another week","She asked the keeper to promise permanence","She erased the rumours by hand"],"correctAnswer":"She walked the alley at dusk and named the doors","explanation":"She walked the alley at dusk, naming each door, and the ink returned by morning.","supportingSentence":"She walked it at dusk, naming each door, and the ink returned by morning.","skill":"detail"},{"question":"What follows from the map recording use rather than promising that places remain?","options":["Naming doors made the ink fade faster","The keeper redrew the city by hand each night","Every street was guaranteed to survive the dawn","A place unused could disappear from the record"],"correctAnswer":"A place unused could disappear from the record","explanation":"If the map records use and does not promise that places remain, an unused street can vanish from it.","supportingSentence":"The keeper said the map recorded use, not a promise that places would remain.","skill":"inference"},{"question":"What does redrew mean in the opening?","options":["Turned a road into a spoken story","Added a loop to an evening route","Drew the map again in a new version","Walked a street at dusk"],"correctAnswer":"Drew the map again in a new version","explanation":"The map redrew itself, meaning it drew its streets again, dropping those nobody had walked.","supportingSentence":"The tower map redrew itself each dawn and forgot any street nobody had walked the previous day.","skill":"vocabulary"},{"question":"Why does the writer include Lale’s evening loop?","options":["To prove the map stopped changing at dusk","To show she began protecting quiet streets by using them","To argue that towers should close at dawn","To suggest rumours are more accurate than ink"],"correctAnswer":"To show she began protecting quiet streets by using them","explanation":"Adding the unwalked streets to her loop shows she started using them so the map would keep them.","supportingSentence":"She added them to a short evening loop.","skill":"intent"}],"wordCount":66,"questionCount":5}$q23253$::jsonb,
  'afc88a0a439d51377d78facd5d49f78069567a391a1c09e970b712f4e98dae89',
  true
) on conflict (content_hash) do nothing;
